div.p:
It is the desire and intention of the Federal Republic not to build a military machine, nor to create forces which are in fact military or para-military, nor to develop its economic capacity for military production, other than or beyond what is necessary to provide for its agreed contribution to defence through the European Defence Community. Accordingly, not only by reason of the foregoing intention, but also for strategic and tactical considerations, the Federal Government will not regard as discriminatory any decision by the European Defence Commission not to allocate for production in Germany
weapons and instruments of warfare, and more especially those in the fields of:
atomic, biological and chemical weapons;
long range and guided missiles;
military (and civil) aircraft;
naval vessels other than minor defensive craft;
(gun barrels of more than 105 mm, and propellents)
